# Driver app environment template. Copy to .env for local overrides.
#
# WARNING: Expo inlines every EXPO_PUBLIC_-prefixed variable into the app bundle.
# Anything here is PUBLIC and shipped to every device. Never put a secret, token
# or password in this file. Auth tokens will live in expo-secure-store.
# See docs/SECURITY.md section 5.
#
# Usually you do NOT need to set this. The app derives the backend host from the
# Expo dev server address, which already works on a physical phone. Set it only
# to override, e.g. for an Android emulator:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8000
#
# A NATIVE build (prebuild / expo run:android / eas build) permits plain HTTP
# only as the lan-demo variant: set NER_BUILD_PROFILE=lan-demo as well, which
# also renames the app "RASTA AI LAN DEMO" with its own package (SEC-007).
# Without it the build has no cleartext exemption, and a named release profile
# with an http:// base is refused. Never ship a lan-demo build.

# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.6:8000
